{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "urn:hsvg:2.0:schema:capability:synth",
  "title": "HyperSVG 2.0 capability synth: Synth",
  "description": "addons.synth.mouth: on a scene or a component (a character speaks for itself, 6.11), the loudness of the voice moves one part: target, else the part of the block's mouth key. Without channel, the part takes the look closed, small, open or round (looks of that part, all drawn); with channel (rotate, translate-x, translate-y, scale, scale-x, scale-y, opacity), the four bands are numbers for that motion channel, inside the part's range. when, a boolean formula of the block (default true), says while it listens: a scene passes a character speaking: true while that character talks. Read every 25 ms | thresholds default smallThreshold 0.025, openThreshold 0.09, roundThreshold 0.18; small is below open and open below round; attack is immediate and releaseMs (default 80) smooths the way back; a muted, silent or hidden voice closes the mouth at once; this is a loudness band, not phoneme detection; the words are always also shown as captions | reduced motion does not change sound",
  "$comment": "Generated by docs/spec-2.0-work/tools/schema/make-schemas.mjs from the spec/2.0 machine files. Do not edit.",
